     1	# The tax is per pair and the meter is cycle length: the loop cost explained — Cycle 921
     2	
     3	Date: 2026-08-05
     4	
     5	Authority: none
     6	
     7	Audit: unset
     8	
     9	Status: bounded worked result (owner-directed mass-lane closure,
    10	window 2b; no axiom surface touched). The loop cost that Cycles 917
    11	and 919 measured and could not explain is EXPLAINED, as a measured
    12	law — and it was never a loop-count law. The surviving mechanism is
    13	the PAIR-CYCLE LAW: the tax is levied per fragment-pair, graded by
    14	the length of the shortest pointer-through cycle joining the pair's
    15	anchors; loop COUNT is refuted outright (ten loops can cost
    16	nothing), and loop POSITION reduces to a binary through-the-pointer
    17	gate already contained in the length axis. One exception — the
    18	degree-2 chain at the high field — is reported as an unexplained
    19	second channel, not absorbed.
    20	
    21	Claim type: bounded_theorem
    22	
    23	Runners:
    24	
    25	- [`frontier_cycle921_loop_cost_2026_07_28.py`](../scripts/frontier_cycle921_loop_cost_2026_07_28.py)
    26	- [`frontier_cycle921_loop_cost_independent_check_2026_07_28.py`](../scripts/frontier_cycle921_loop_cost_independent_check_2026_07_28.py)
    27	
