    36	
    37	Worker disclosure: authored by a Claude Opus 5 worker under supervisor
    38	spec (substitution disclosed). Both readings of "loop count" were run
    39	(linear and fitted-half cyclomatic), neither silently dropped. One
    40	receipt defect found by the checker is documented rather than hidden:
    41	fragment pairs are keyed under two orderings (one inherited from the
    42	pinned 917 receipt, which cannot change without breaking the
    43	value-for-value gate; one in declared label order) — content verified
    44	identical on all geometries by canonical comparison; downstream
    45	readers must key on the unordered pair. Independent audit still
    46	required.
    47	
    48	## The design idea, and the candidate set
    49	
    50	Nine candidate mechanisms plus five degeneracy probes, each reduced
    51	to an INTEGER PREDICTOR that is a pure function of the graph and the
    52	frozen partition, computed BEFORE any propagator runs — nothing is
    53	fitted after the fact. The controlling observation: the frozen
    54	partition rule makes every pointer neighbour the anchor of its own
    55	fragment, so a cycle through the pointer joins two anchors, and the
    56	anchor-to-anchor distance d in G with the pointer deleted is exactly
    57	(cycle length - 2). The designed families sweep d at fixed pointer
    58	degree. 32 designed geometries + the 10 pinned 917/919 anchors = 42
    59	geometries at the three declared fields (126 declared cells), plus
    60	64 non-claim probe cells at higher fields.
    61	
    62	## The measurement
    63	
    64	Restriction gates at exactly zero deviation before any new number:
    65	917 reproduced value-for-value (12 cells, 156 rows, all deviations
    66	exactly 0) AND the 919 anchors reproduced the same way (H4's
    67	5 / 3 / 3 ceiling profile exact); 21/21 frozen constants
    68	byte-verified, quote-identical to both pinned receipts; the
    69	partition rule reproduces the memo's own six cube fragment lists.
    70	Routes: Chebyshev/Bessel (tail 3.7e-18) vs scaling-and-marching
    71	Taylor (remainder 8.8e-20) at 6.8e-14; dense eigendecomposition at
    72	6.9e-14 where n <= 12; deterministic double-run with identical
    73	receipt content digest.
    74	
    75	**The decisive matched pairs** (lambda = 0.10): two pairs of
    76	designed geometries are identical on EVERY statistic the machinery
    77	tracks — sites, bonds, loops, seams, degree, max degree, depth,
    78	components, the fragment-size multiset — and still split their
    79	ceilings 4 against 3. No function of those counts can produce that
    80	split; only the anchor distance differs. The seam-count and
    81	loop-count ladders hold the pair set fixed while loop count rises —
    82	the ceiling never moves (ten-loop QB10 pays nothing; four internal
    83	loops pay nothing).
    84	
    85	**Margins are wide, unlike the persistence boundary**: at the high
    86	field the d=2 pairs clear the dependence gate by ~ +0.016 bits and
    87	the d=3 pairs miss by ~ -0.010 bits — a factor-of-two separation on
    88	the gate, not a razor.
    89	
    90	## The pair-cycle law
    91	
    92	For each pair of pointer-fragments (a, b), let d(a, b) be the
    93	distance between their anchors in G with the pointer deleted (the
    94	shortest pointer-through cycle containing both anchors has length
    95	d + 2). Over the frozen certification window:
    96	
    97	- **d = 1** (cycle length 3): removes BOTH fragments — they fail
    98	  the content gate at every measured field;
    99	- **d = 2** (cycle length 4, the lattice plaquette): removes the
   100	  PAIR from mutual independence at lambda >= 0.075, but not at
   101	  0.05;
   102	- **d >= 3** (cycle length >= 5): costs nothing at any measured
   103	  field;
   104	
   105	and **max R_ind = the independence number of what survives.** A
   106	loop-free geometry has no finite d, so the ceiling equals pointer
   107	degree — exactly Cycle 917's reading — and 917's high-field loopy
   108	failures are exactly its d = 2 pairs. The crossover field is
   109	monotone in d (d = 1 over at 0.05; d = 2 crosses in (0.05, 0.075];
   110	d = 3 near 0.15; d >= 5 never in range — probe-grade).
   111	
   112	**Discrimination**: the law scores 42/42, 42/42, 41/42 exact at the
   113	three fields (32/32 on every geometry this block designed); the
   114	best rival reaches 34/42 — and it is a degeneracy probe (the
   115	Koenig/matching bound, separated by the odd-cycle pair graphs), not
   116	a mechanism. Loop-count is refuted in both readings; seam monogamy
   117	predicts 1 where 5 is measured; position candidates die on QP1 and
   118	QW1.
   119	
   120	**The three axes, answered**: LENGTH is decisive and sets the
   121	regime. COUNT is not decisive (six ladders, ceiling unchanged in
   122	every one). POSITION is decisive only as the binary
   123	through-the-pointer gate — a loop that avoids the pointer costs
   124	nothing however many and however close (four internal loops,
   125	ceiling intact), and once a loop passes through the pointer its
   126	distance IS its length.
   127	
   128	## The exception, reported
   129	
   130	917's degree-2 chain G1 at lambda = 0.10: predicted 2, measured 1.
   131	Its two arms sit at infinite anchor distance, so the law predicts
   132	no cost — the drop comes from a SECOND, loop-independent channel
   133	that grows with fragment size and field (the 4-site arms reach
   134	C_ab = 0.0217, just over the 0.02 gate). This block does not
   135	explain that channel; it is the named successor (running as Cycle
   136	927).
   137	
   138	## Scope findings (structural, disclosed)
   139	
   140	- Under the frozen partition rule, a site adjacent to two anchors
   141	  is necessarily equidistant from both, so **anchor distance 2 is
   142	  only constructible in cube coordinates**, where the memo's
   143	  tie-break is defined: the field-graded d = 2 regime CANNOT appear
   144	  on any tie-free geometry. A property of the frozen rule, not a
   145	  design choice.
   146	- A length-3 pointer cycle necessarily joins two recording sites,
   147	  both prepared +X — structurally forced, not a confound.
   148	- One design-extension-field cell (QC8 at 0.075) has a d = 2 pair
