   189	target_claim_type: bounded_theorem
   190	conditional_surface_status: "the law is at the frozen gates and fields (the crossover-field ladder is probe-grade outside the frozen set); anchor distance 2 is constructible only in cube coordinates under the frozen tie-break (structural scope rule); the G1 chain exception is carried openly (predicted 2, measured 1 — the second channel); pair keys appear under two orderings in the receipt (documented; key on the unordered pair)"
   191	hypothetical_axiom_status: null
   192	admitted_observation_status: null
   193	claim_type_reason: "every predictor is a pre-registered integer function of the graph computed before any propagator ran; two matched pairs identical on every tracked statistic still split, excluding all counting mechanisms at once; the law is exact on 32/32 designed geometries with the margins wide (not a persistence razor); the checker's 120-cell adversarial hunt and 102-geometry degeneracy attack leave no rival within 8 cells; both restriction surfaces reproduced at deviation exactly 0 first"
   194	audit_required_before_effective_retained: true
   195	bare_retained_allowed: false
   196	```
   197	
   198	## Imports, derived, open
   199	
   200	### Imports
   201	
   202	- the three frozen memos (gates and partition rule, verbatim), the
   203	  917/919 primaries + receipts (the anchors and constants
   204	  authority, both reproduced at zero), the axiom memo (pinned);
   205	  the G6 row via pinned receipts (not re-run).
   206	
   207	### Derived
   208	
   209	- the pair-cycle law with its three-tier grading and the
   210	  ceiling-as-independence-number composition;
   211	- the refutation of loop-count (both readings) and the reduction
   212	  of position to the through-pointer gate;
   213	- the matched-pair exclusion of every counting mechanism;
   214	- the crossover-field ladder in d (probe-grade);
   215	- the G1 exception as a second channel (named, unexplained);
   216	- the structural scope rules (d = 2 needs cube coordinates; l = 3
   217	  forces +X/+X).
   218	
   219	### Open
   220	
   221	- the size-driven second channel (G1's drop — Cycle 927, running);
   222	- the lambda*(d = 2) bisection; the QC8 extension cell;
   223	- the tie-free-geometry question (whether any tie-break extension
   224	  admits d = 2 off the cube — a frozen-rule question, not this
   225	  block's);
   226	- the audit-lane propagation: retire loop-count phrasing wherever
   227	  cited.
   228	
   229	## Verdict
   230	
   231	Two cycles measured that loops cost redundancy and left the reason
   232	standing as a slogan; this block replaces the slogan with a meter.
   233	The cost was never about how many loops a geometry carries — ten
   234	can be free — and never about where they sit, except as the single
   235	question of whether they pass through the pointer. What matters is
   236	the length of the cycle a pair of records shares: three sites and
   237	both records die of contamination, four and the pair merely stops
   238	being independent once the field is high enough, five or more and
   239	the loop is invisible. The ceiling the earlier cycles wrote as a
   240	degree with corrections becomes one clean sentence — the
   241	independence number of what the cycles leave alive — and the one
   242	geometry the sentence cannot cover is promoted, not buried: the
   243	chain's quiet second channel is already on the bench as the next
   244	measurement. Independent audit still required.

