    47	expression, never of value: it induces a singleton on scopes. SL1b
    48	was never open as a family question, only as an expression question.
    49	(Also recorded: 883's docstring says "four" closed forms; its own
    50	certificate computed five — stale prose, current computation, nothing
    51	downstream moves.)
    52	
    53	## The native table (Q1/Q4, complete over the canonical scopes)
    54	
    55	| scope | n | K_native | F_dim | F_res | F_ded |
    56	|---|---|---|---|---|---|
    57	| C2_face | 2 | **1/4** | 1/4 | 1/8 | 0 |
    58	| C2_edge | 2 | **1/4** | 1/4 | 1/8 | 0 |
    59	| C3_body | 3 | **2/9** | 2/9 | 2/9 | 2/9 |
    60	| C4_face | 4 | **3/16** | 3/16 | 5/16 | 1/2 |
    61	| V_edge | 4 | **3/16** | 3/16 | 5/16 | 1/2 |
    62	| S3_body | 6 | 5/36 (not canonical) | 5/36 | 35/72 | 10/9 |
    63	
    64	**The construction binds to F_dim** — at every canonical scope, with
    65	the C3 restriction gate reproducing 2/9 name-for-name against the
    66	pinned 883 cache first. Note that n = 2 ALREADY discriminates (1/4
    67	vs 1/8 vs 0) — the sibling fork note's "diverge at N=4" understates
    68	the discrimination surface.
    69	
    70	## The retained arithmetic diverges — and WHY (Q2)
    71	
    72	The retained L-face, rebuilt from its own recipe (the transverse
    73	determinant sum), reads 2/9 at C3 and **5/16 at C4** — the F_res
    74	family, DERIVED for N = 2..12 by exact trace-of-inverse in the
    75	cyclotomic quotient ring, not assumed. The disagreement is **about
    76	which SPACE, not which functional**: transported onto the readout
    77	module where the derivation lives, the note's recipe is defined only
    78	at prime orbit length and there equals F_dim; at C4 it divides by
    79	zero on the sign summand the geometric normal plane does not have.
    80	N = 3 is the UNIQUE length where the geometric normal plane and the
    81	readout transverse space are isomorphic (both the 2-dimensional
    82	rational irrep of C3) — the same uniqueness the K_3 = C_3 finding
    83	expresses on the graph side. V_edge and S3 have zero-dimensional
    84	common fixed space, so the fixed-locus/normal split does not exist
    85	there at all.
    86	
    87	**The entire residual is one identification**: does the record read
    88	the readout module's invariant complement (then the anchor family is
    89	F_dim, and at C4 the readout is 3/16) or the lattice rotation's
    90	geometric normal plane (then F_res, 5/16)? Decidable at C4; the
    91	falsification route is named (show the record reads the geometric
    92	plane and the verdict flips without touching any computation here).
    93	
    94	## The no-family result, quantified (Q3, empirically clean)
    95	
    96	Zero members of the declared family/transform space fall inside the
    97	fitted-delta enclosure. Nearest member: distance 1.95e-9; nearest
    98	bare family value: 2/9 itself at 1.75e-7; any rational inside the
    99	enclosure needs denominator >= 700,358,457 (Stern-Brocot, agreeing
   100	with the checker's continued fractions). The fitted number is not a
   101	retained family value, quantified.
   102	
   103	## Checker
   104	
   105	12/12 claims survive; 9/9 teeth; zero blind spots. On the crux —
   106	recipe identifiability — an independent whole-module scan recovered
   107	exactly the same seven expressions, the same five hits, the same
   108	F_dim binding: not refuted. Its sharpest adversarial result is the
   109	method's own honesty bound: **402 monomial-quotient forms return 2/9
   110	at C3, taking 10 distinct values at C4** — agreement at the pinned
   111	scope constrains almost nothing, and what is family-identified is
   112	the form set 883 actually wrote, evaluated off-scope. The Q3 attack
   113	(Mobius bound, cross-family products and ratios, powers) found
   114	nothing inside the enclosure.
