Two more blockers are confirmed. Twenty changed runners pin the superseded pre-main axiom bytes, and the Cycle 916 “re-execution” requires nine Git blobs plus two commits that are not reachable from `origin/main`; a normal audit clone cannot reproduce it. I’m recording those as compatibility failures, not treating local object-cache success as reproducibility.
